  "notes": {
   "linuxserver": "**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/linuxserver-playground/docker-piper/compare/2.5.2-ls8...2.5.3-ls9",
   "upstream": "- Update `voices.json`: 6 new voices, 36 updated. The Japanese voice is now\n  `ja_JP-hi_fi_captain-medium`; the old `ja_JA-hi_fi_captain-medium` name is\n  kept as an alias\n- Add `--upload-dir`, where the web UI saves uploaded Piper voices (default:\n  `--download-dir`, as before). Uploads and catalog downloads used to share\n  `--download-dir`, so a backup could not include the irreplaceable uploads\n  without also carrying every re-downloadable catalog voice (20-110 MB each).\n  With separate directories, the download directory can be left out of backups\n  whole. An upload directory that is not a `--data-dir` is searched before\n  all of them, so uploads are always found and a custom voice wins over a\n  catalog voice of the same name\n- Answer a plain `synthesize` sent on the same connection after a text stream.\n  The streaming flag set by `synthesize-start` was never cleared, so every later\n  `synthesize` was skipped as a compatibility copy and the client waited for an\n  `audio-stop` that never came",
   "upstream_url": "https://github.com/OHF-Voice/wyoming-piper/releases/tag/v2.5.3"
  },
